+/-! # A common denominator for the point of the pinned clipping system
+
+This file is an addition to the upstream development. It repeats the tight-rank and
+Cramer argument of `ProjectionCramer` / `ProjectionSmallPoint` for the system that
+pins the committed generator coordinates, with three refinements.
+
+* The committed coordinates are integers `z j` over one positive integer `q` (they are
+  produced by normalizing an integer vector by its last coordinate). The pin rows
+  `y (anchor j) = z j / q` are therefore not cleared at all: the system is solved for
+  `q • y`, whose right-hand side is integral.
+* Only the right-hand side then carries the commitment height `G`. Expanding Cramer's
+  numerators along the replaced column (through the adjugate), the determinants are
+  bounded by `(s + 1)! * (B ^ (s + 2)) ^ (s + 1) * G`: the commitment height enters
+  once, where the upstream bound `s! * ((B + G + 1) ^ (s + 2)) ^ s` has it to the power
+  `s * (s + 2)`.
+* Cramer's rule gives all coordinates over the one denominator `q * det`. An affine form
+  evaluated at such a point has height `(s + 1) * (C + 1) ^ (s + 2) * Y` instead of
+  `(s + 1) * ((C + 1) * (Y + 1)) ^ (s + 2)`: the height `Y` of the point enters once, not
+  once for every coordinate.
+-/
+
